    },
    "html": "\n        <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n          <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n          <span class=\"time\">30 min</span>\n          <span class=\"chip company\">Amazon</span><span class=\"chip company\">Microsoft</span><span class=\"chip company\">Walmart</span><span class=\"chip company\">Flipkart</span>\n        </div>\n        <h1>URL Shortener (TinyURL)</h1>\n        <p class=\"lead\">This is the most common \"first\" system design question. After this page you can turn a long link into a 7-character code, explain why reads outnumber writes 100 to 1, do the maths in under 3 minutes, and handle the follow-ups: \"how do two servers not make the same code?\", \"301 or 302?\" and \"how do you count clicks?\"</p>\n      "
